    "body": "## What changed\n- require a persisted authenticated actor before Stripe top-up creation and refund request/read operations\n- reject missing or transient principals before invoking financial services\n- add controller regressions asserting zero payment/refund service interactions for invalid identity\n- document the fail-closed payment identity boundary\n\n## Security / financial rationale\nThese endpoints previously dereferenced `user.getId()` directly. Missing or non-persistent identity could therefore degrade into an NPE at a financial boundary rather than a controlled authorization failure. Financial operations now fail closed before any payment/refund service call.\n\n## Validation gate\nDo not merge unless all relevant checks are green for the exact PR head SHA, review threads are clear, and `master` has not moved (or the branch is safely rebased first).",
